    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"What Determines Women's Employment in Urban Slums?\"\nsubtitle: \"Role of Marital Status, Family Structure, and Age\"\nauthor: \"Ramesh Beniwal\"\ndate: today\nformat:\n  revealjs:\n    theme: white\n    transition: slide\n    background-transition: fade\n    slide-number: true\n    chalkboard: false\n    footer: \"Women's Employment Analysis | Urban Slums 2026\"\n    width: 1920\n    height: 1200\n    margin: 0.04\n    embed-resources: true\nexecute:\n  warning: false\n  message: false\n  echo: false\n  fig-width: 18\n  fig-height: 8\n  fig-align: center\neditor:\n  markdown:\n    wrap: 72\n---\n\n\n\n\n\n## Introduction {.center}\n\n::::::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"52%\"}\n\n### Motivation {style=\"font-size: 1.3em;\"}\n\n::: {style=\"font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 2.0; margin-top: 20px;\"}\n- Women's employment is a key indicator of **empowerment** and household welfare\n- Urban slum women face multiple barriers — family structure, marital status, and social norms\n- Very few studies focus on determinants of employment among slum women in India\n- This study uses data from **four urban slums** — Atal Ayub Nagar, Nawab Colony, J.P Nagar, Arif Nagar\n:::\n::::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"48%\"}\n\n### Research Question {style=\"font-size: 1.3em;\"}\n\n::: {style=\"font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.9; background-color: #dceeff; padding: 25px; border-left: 6px solid #2c7fb8; border-radius: 6px; margin-top: 20px;\"}\n*\"What determines women's employment in urban slums — role of marital status, family structure, and age?\"*\n:::\n\n::: {style=\"font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 2.2; margin-top: 25px;\"}\n- **Dependent:** Currently Working (Yes/No)\n- **Independent:** Marital Status, Family Type, Age\n- **Controls:** Education, In-laws Alive\n:::\n::::\n:::::::\n\n---\n\n\n## Data Cleaning {.center}\n\n::: {style=\"font-size: 1.2em; line-height: 2.2; padding: 10px 60px; margin-top: 10px;\"}\n- Data collected from **four urban slums** in 2026\n\n- Age = 0 replaced with **NA** &nbsp;— data entry error\n\n- Education > 16 replaced with **NA** &nbsp;— beyond questionnaire range\n\n- Marital status recoded: **Widowed / Separated = 1**, others = 0\n\n- Education grouped into six categories: **Illiterate, Primary, Middle, Secondary, Higher Secondary, Graduate & Above**\n\n- Age grouped into six categories: **18–24, 25–34, 35–44, 45–54, 55–64, 65+**\n\n- **Binary dummies** created for each education and age category\n:::\n\n---\n\n\n## Summary Statistics (Slums) {.center}\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-hover table-condensed\" style=\"font-size: 22px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: rgba(44, 127, 184, 1) !important;font-size: 23px;\"> Variable </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: rgba(44, 127, 184, 1) !important;font-size: 23px;\"> N </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: rgba(44, 127, 184, 1) !important;font-size: 23px;\"> Mean </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: rgba(44, 127, 184, 1) !important;font-size: 23px;\"> Std. Dev. </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: rgba(44, 127, 184, 1) !important;font-size: 23px;\"> Min </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: rgba(44, 127, 184, 1) !important;font-size: 23px;\"> Max </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;width: 50%; font-weight: bold;color: black !important;background-color: rgba(208, 228, 247, 1) !important;font-size: 23px;\"> Panel A: Dependent Variable </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;width: 10%; font-weight: bold;color: black !important;background-c